  "findings": [
    "Inspected 2017 and March 2018 Blimpy readers decode packed SIGPROC angles by absolute magnitude followed by sign, and treat HDF5 declination as decimal degrees.",
    "The pre-scan May 2016 guppi2spectra.c takes DEC_STR, concatenates degree/minute fields and left-pads its seconds field before strtod. Later inspected code retains that mechanism. The original selected DEC_STR is unavailable.",
    "The original GUPPI status code uses SLALIB sign and sexagesimal fields; the later Ruby status code separates the negative sign before formatting. Neither inspected path establishes a file-specific correction.",
    "No exact selected-session source hit was returned by the bounded GitHub code search. This is not proof that a public log does not exist.",
    "No executable deployed version, same-scan RAW header, observing log, or documented transform was found that resolves the retained three ON declinations."
  ],
  "status": "HOLD_POINTING_PROVENANCE_UNRESOLVED",
